@startuml 02-add-items-to-project
title Scenario 2: Add items to a project for the first time

actor User
participant "Claude Code\nsession" as Claude
participant "catalog skill" as Skill
participant "catalog.sh" as Cat
participant "GitHub\n(Eminakkoc/skills)" as Index
participant "Upstream sources\n(GitHub / npm)" as Up
database "<project>/.claude\n+ .mcp.json" as Proj
database "<U+007E>/.claude" as Home

User -> Claude : "add the web bundle to this project"
Claude -> Skill : load (request matches catalog skill)
Skill --> Claude : run catalog.sh, never edit\nsettings or lock files by hand
Claude -> Cat : catalog add bundle:web

== Resolve ==
Cat -> Index : resolve main -> SHA, fetch catalog/ + sources.json
Index --> Cat : index @ SHA
Cat -> Cat : expand bundle into items
Cat -> Cat : check scope of each item
alt item has scope = user (and no --force)
  Cat --> Claude : refuse that item\n("user item, install with --user")
end
Cat -> Cat : resolve "requires"
opt a required tool is missing (e.g. agent-browser CLI)
  Cat -> Up : install tool @ pinned (user scope)
  Cat -> Home : record in <U+007E>/.claude/catalog.lock.json
end

== Install into the project ==
loop each project item
  alt kind = skill
    Cat -> Up : fetch <repo> @ <pinned SHA>\n(or this repo @ index SHA for own items)
    Cat -> Proj : write .claude/skills/<name>/
  else kind = hook
    Cat -> Proj : write .claude/hooks/<name>/<script>
    Cat -> Proj : merge entry into .claude/settings.json\n(command = "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"/.claude/hooks/...)
  else kind = mcp
    Cat -> Proj : merge server into .mcp.json\n(npx <package>@<pinned> for npm servers)
  else kind = plugin
    Cat -> Proj : add extraKnownMarketplaces + enabledPlugins\nto .claude/settings.json
  end
  Cat -> Proj : record item in .claude/catalog.lock.json
end

Cat --> Claude : summary: files written, settings merged
Claude --> User : show changes, suggest committing\n.claude/ and .mcp.json

== Next session ==
User -> Claude : restart claude in the project
Claude -> Proj : load project skills and hooks
Claude --> User : prompt to approve project MCP servers\nand install enabled plugins
@enduml
